  "task": {
    "objective": "Transport four complementary parcels to their bilateral private target depots by negotiating scarce expiring bridge access; choose toll revenue, prompt passage and reciprocal delivery assistance.",
    "natural_termination": "Terminate when all four unique parcels have been delivered. Otherwise truncate at 160; undelivered demands remain explicitly unsatisfied.",
    "interaction": "Each issuer must use the other bridge to cross; neither can issue itself a permit. A grant escrows a scarce real token and an action near a control point. Permits constrain entering the only river crossings. Toll quotes, expiry, physical congestion and complementary recipient rewards create cross-agent opportunities and costs.",
